{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 694 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D7"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the lorazepam injection shortage on 2018-05-03 and it remains Current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E35", "E31", "E32", "E33", "E34"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our Corvale General and Corvale East sites both use Hospira, Inc. product (NDC 00409198530) for the 2 mg/mL, 1 mL presentation.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hospira plant (FEI 1925262) received an OAI classification from an inspection that ended 2016-06-08, which was 694 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["E12", "D7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Warning Letter was issued to the same plant on 2017-02-14, 443 days before the posting, and a later inspection ending 2018-08-15 was classified OAI with a classification letter dated 2020-04-22.",
      "cites": ["E17", "D9", "E14", "D15"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 3.4 days on hand of the 2 mg/mL, 1 mL product while Corvale General has 14.6 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked option by rule is to transfer 4 units of 2 mg/mL, 1 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would bring Corvale East to 4 days on hand while Corvale General retains two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D17"]
    }
  ]
}
